{"name":"Siren","hex":"#69293b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Siren","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Sirenidae – certain sirens."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village, the county seat of Burnett County, Wisconsin, United States.","A town in Burnett County, Wisconsin, United States, surrounding the village of the same name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Siren"}],"entries":[{"title":"Siren (alarm)","blocks":[{"text":"A siren is a noise-making warning device. There are two general types: mechanical sirens and electronic sirens. Civil defense sirens are mounted in fixed locations and used to warn of natural disasters or attacks. Sirens are used on emergency service vehicles such as ambulances, police cars, and fire engines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Electronic_Sirens_Pavian_by_Telegrafia.jpg/330px-Electronic_Sirens_Pavian_by_Telegrafia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siren_(alarm)"},{"title":"Siren (mythology)","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, sirens are female humanlike beings with alluring voices; they appear in a scene in the Odyssey in which Odysseus saves his crew's lives. Roman poets place them on some small islands called Sirenum Scopuli. In some later, rationalized traditions, the literal geography of the \"flowery\" island of Anthemoessa, or Anthemusa, is fixed: sometimes on Cape Pelorum and at others in the islands known as the Sirenuse, near Paestum, or in Capreae. All such locations were surrounded by cliffs and rocks. While some versions have depicted Sirens as woman-headed birds, other versions depict them as mermaids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/NAMA_Sir%C3%A8ne.jpg/330px-NAMA_Sir%C3%A8ne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siren_(mythology)"},{"title":"Siren (2016 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Siren is a 2016 American supernatural horror film directed by Gregg Bishop and written by Ben Collins and Luke Piotrowski. It is the first spin-off film in the V/H/S franchise and feature-length adaptation of \"Amateur Night\", David Bruckner's segment from the 2012 film V/H/S. The film focuses on Jonah and his groomsmen the day before his wedding, as they embark on a wild night of partying and debauchery. The party, however, becomes a savage fight for survival when they unwittingly unleash a fabled predator upon the festivities."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Siren_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siren_(2016_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/TWS_295_Sirens%2C_Saudi_Arabia_Warning_System.jpg/500px-TWS_295_Sirens%2C_Saudi_Arabia_Warning_System.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/TWS_295_Sirens%2C_Saudi_Arabia_Warning_System.jpg/1280px-TWS_295_Sirens%2C_Saudi_Arabia_Warning_System.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/TWS_295_Sirens%2C_Saudi_Arabia_Warning_System.jpg/500px-TWS_295_Sirens%2C_Saudi_Arabia_Warning_System.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Whelen WPS-2805 electronic siren imported to Saudi Arabia by HSS Engineering for use as a civil defense siren.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATWS_295_Sirens%2C_Saudi_Arabia_Warning_System.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Picswiss_BL-56-08.jpg/250px-Picswiss_BL-56-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/48/Picswiss_BL-56-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Picswiss_BL-56-08.jpg/250px-Picswiss_BL-56-08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"There are 8,200 alarm sirens for civil protection throughout Switzerland. They are tested once a year, on the first Wednesday of February.[1] Sound sampleⓘ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APicswiss_BL-56-08.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Siren_%28Harper%27s_Engraving%29.png/500px-Siren_%28Harper%27s_Engraving%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Siren_%28Harper%27s_Engraving%29.png/1280px-Siren_%28Harper%27s_Engraving%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Siren_%28Harper%27s_Engraving%29.png/500px-Siren_%28Harper%27s_Engraving%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The world's first siren, from the 1860s.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASiren_(Harper's_Engraving).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Lowestoft_siren.jpg/500px-Lowestoft_siren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Lowestoft_siren.jpg/1280px-Lowestoft_siren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Lowestoft_siren.jpg/500px-Lowestoft_siren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The air raid siren used to alert the town of Lowe­stoft during World War II.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.